  "description": "The link offer after a redirect sign-in (I-43.2, WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.11.4). A token exchange found no link for the person's Apple identity and answered a link handle. The person then signs in on this device through the browser (authorize, Continue, token): that same-device sign-in leaves a step-up that lasts 300 s. GET link, with the device token, names the kinds the person could add (reach null until a link is made). A POST link carrying the handle and a pkey-proof/1 link proof by the device's key, sent after the step-up went stale, is 401 step_up_required and leaves the handle where it is. After a fresh sign-in the same POST answers linked {kind, reach}: an Apple link is scoped to the developer's team. The link spends the step-up, so the offer is empty afterwards.",
